WEBVTT

00:00:01.630 --> 00:00:06.500
Marcel and the Mona Lisa by Stephen Rabley.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.478
Marcel is a French mouse and a detective.

00:00:11.538 --> 00:00:13.890
He has lots of friends in Paris.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.500
One of them is Céline.

00:00:16.602 --> 00:00:20.155
She paints pictures and is very beautiful.

00:00:20.215 --> 00:00:23.748
Céline's home is at the Louvre.

00:00:23.808 --> 00:00:26.842
Marcel often goes there for dinner.

00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:30.850
One evening in May he arrives with some pink flowers.

00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:33.148
There is a guard at the door.

00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:35.092
"I don't know him," 

00:00:35.152 --> 00:00:38.315
Marcel thinks. "He must be new."

00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:40.408
Then he walks inside.

00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:44.820
The two friends eat, drink and talk all evening.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.391
Céline shows Marcel her new paintings.

00:00:48.451 --> 00:00:52.333
They talk about their summer holiday in Los Angeles.

00:00:52.393 --> 00:00:58.065
They laugh, play jazz records and tell lots of stories.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:01:03.197
Then at 11 o'clock Marcel puts on his coat.

00:01:03.257 --> 00:01:05.528
"It's late," he says.

00:01:05.588 --> 00:01:06.900
"I must go home."

00:01:07.249 --> 00:01:09.670
Two minutes later he leaves.

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.300
"Good night," says Céline. 

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.774
Then she closes her front door.

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:19.067
Marcel walks across the floor. He is very happy.

00:01:19.127 --> 00:01:20.558
Then he stops.

00:01:20.618 --> 00:01:24.972
The room is dark, but he can see something.

00:01:25.032 --> 00:01:26.182
What is it?

00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:27.033
A man?

00:01:27.753 --> 00:01:30.246
A man with a long knife?

00:01:30.306 --> 00:01:31.726
Yes!

00:01:31.786 --> 00:01:34.900
Suddenly Marcel's mouth is very dry.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.500
He runs to the wall.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.530
Then, after five seconds, he looks again.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.700
This time he can see the man's face.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:46.492
"It's that new guard," he thinks.

00:01:46.552 --> 00:01:50.427
"And he's... he's stealing the Mona Lisa!"

00:01:50.487 --> 00:01:54.512
Next to the thief there is a black bag.

00:01:54.572 --> 00:01:58.976
Two minutes later the Mona Lisa is inside it.

00:01:59.036 --> 00:02:02.229
The thief smiles and picks up the bag.

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:06.492
But a second later he puts it down again.

00:02:06.552 --> 00:02:12.910
"Car keys," he says, and begins to look in all his pockets.

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:14.962
"All right..."

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.294
"This is it," Marcel thinks.

00:02:17.354 --> 00:02:19.154
"It's now or never."

00:02:19.214 --> 00:02:21.900
He runs along the wall very fast, 

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:26.209
climbs up the tall, black bag and jumps inside it.

00:02:26.268 --> 00:02:30.550
At the bottom of the bag Marcel can see a face.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.972
The Mona Lisa's face.

00:02:33.032 --> 00:02:35.694
She is smiling at him.

00:02:35.754 --> 00:02:38.848
"Now what?" he asks her.
  
00:02:38.908 --> 00:02:44.492
There is no answer, but at that moment the bag starts to move.

00:02:44.552 --> 00:02:48.166
Marcel can hear lots of noises.

00:02:48.225 --> 00:02:50.017
A motor starts.

00:02:50.077 --> 00:02:52.369
Traffic goes by.

00:02:52.429 --> 00:02:54.181
A radio plays.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.992
Then the bag suddenly stops.

00:02:57.052 --> 00:03:03.700
Marcel climbs the painting and looks out. "A railway station!"

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:08.669
Five minutes later the Louvre guard gets on a train.

00:03:08.729 --> 00:03:16.604
He sits next to a thin man in sunglasses and a white jacket.

00:03:16.664 --> 00:03:20.377
"Have you got it, Antoine?"

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:24.810
the thin man asks. "Yes," the guard answers.
 
00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:29.324
After that the train starts and there's a lot of noise.

00:03:29.384 --> 00:03:30.546
"Oh no!

00:03:30.606 --> 00:03:33.678
Now I can't hear them," Marcel thinks.

00:03:33.738 --> 00:03:37.140
But he can hear one or two words.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:44.475
"Italy," for example, and "all those cats. Cats!"
  
00:03:44.535 --> 00:03:47.066
Marcel looks at the Mona Lisa.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:50.479
His eyes are two big saucers.

00:03:50.539 --> 00:03:55.200
"But cats kill mice," he thinks.

00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:56.900
"They eat them.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:05.900
And where are we going? In Italy? Rome? Milan? Naples?"

00:04:06.035 --> 00:04:11.662
But at that moment Antoine puts the bag under the seat.
 
00:04:11.722 --> 00:04:15.996
"Now I really can't hear," Marcel thinks.
 
00:04:16.056 --> 00:04:21.738
Then he goes to sleep and has a very bad dream.

00:04:21.798 --> 00:04:25.867
Early next morning the sun is shining.

00:04:25.926 --> 00:04:29.511
Marcel opens his eyes and sees the Mona Lisa.

00:04:29.570 --> 00:04:32.114
Then he remembers where he is.

00:04:32.174 --> 00:04:37.580
He runs up the painting and looks at Antoine and Henri.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.682
"Good," he thinks. "They're asleep."
  
00:04:41.742 --> 00:04:45.664
Ten seconds later, Marcel is standing at the window.

00:04:45.724 --> 00:04:49.566
He can see a small village and some mountains.

00:04:49.626 --> 00:04:56.580
Then a sign goes by: a hundred and eighty kilometres to Venice!

00:04:56.640 --> 00:05:04.374
Two hours later Antoine and Henri are on a gondola.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:09.186
"Look," says Antoine and laughs. 

00:05:09.246 --> 00:05:12.109
He shows Henri a newspaper story.

00:05:12.169 --> 00:05:17.422
It says, "THIEVES TAKE DA VINCI PAINTING."

00:05:17.482 --> 00:05:24.016
Henri says, "Be quiet!" and turns to the boatman.

00:05:24.076 --> 00:05:27.548
"Do you see that big palace on the left?"

00:05:27.608 --> 00:05:31.010
"Signor Spandini's house?"

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:34.968
"Yes. Stop there."

00:05:35.028 --> 00:05:40.186
Inside the bag Marcel hears every word.

00:05:40.246 --> 00:05:43.228
An old woman answers the front door.

00:05:43.248 --> 00:05:47.900
"Come in," she says to the two thieves.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:52.562
"Signor Spandini is waiting for you."

00:05:52.622 --> 00:05:55.694
She takes them to a big, dark room.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:59.496
A fat man is sitting behind a desk. a desk.

00:05:59.556 --> 00:06:02.800
"Have you got it?" he asks.
 
00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:07.627
"Yes". "Boss" Henri answers.

00:06:07.687 --> 00:06:09.457
The bag is beside him.

00:06:09.517 --> 00:06:12.728
"I can't stay in here," Marcel thinks.

00:06:12.788 --> 00:06:17.150
He jumps out of the bag and hides behind a chair.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.340
"Good," he thinks.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:25.082
"Now I can..." But then he goes cold. "Cats!"
 
00:06:25.142 --> 00:06:28.493
There are seven, eight...
 
00:06:28.553 --> 00:06:31.014
No, nine of them in the room.

00:06:31.074 --> 00:06:36.000
Suddenly Marcel remembers Henri's words.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:39.416
"All those cats!"

00:06:39.476 --> 00:06:42.300
Then he remembers his dream on the train.

00:06:42.397 --> 00:06:44.998
What can he do? Where can he go?

00:06:45.058 --> 00:06:46.518
But it's too late.

00:06:46.578 --> 00:06:48.828
One of the cats sees him.

00:06:48.888 --> 00:06:49.899
"Help!"

00:06:49.959 --> 00:06:53.900
Marcel thinks and climbs up a red curtain.

00:06:53.960 --> 00:06:57.991
A moment later the cat starts climbing, too.

00:06:58.051 --> 00:07:00.400
Marcel can hear it below him.

00:07:00.512 --> 00:07:02.633
He has to do something — and fast!

00:07:02.693 --> 00:07:03.699
But what?

00:07:03.759 --> 00:07:06.850
Then he sees two candles above his head.

00:07:07.056 --> 00:07:09.547
"That's the answer," he thinks.

00:07:09.607 --> 00:07:14.598
He jumps onto the bookcase and starts to push the candles over.
 
00:07:14.658 --> 00:07:19.770
They are very heavy, but in the end he does it.

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:25.982
Below him he hears, "Yeeooowwwww!"

00:07:26.042 --> 00:07:31.222
"What's all that noise?" asks Antoine.

00:07:31.282 --> 00:07:32.952
"Look!

00:07:33.012 --> 00:07:38.174
The carpet's on fire!" says Henri. Spandini stands up.

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:42.095
"Angelina! Quick, bring some water."
 
00:07:42.155 --> 00:07:44.426
Marcel looks over the bookcase.

00:07:44.486 --> 00:07:48.006
He can see the Mona Lisa on Spandini's desk.

00:07:48.066 --> 00:07:49.617
"OK," he thinks.

00:07:49.677 --> 00:07:50.968
"This is it."

00:07:51.028 --> 00:07:53.738
After that he runs down the curtain,

00:07:53.798 --> 00:07:56.000
across Spandini's desk, 

00:07:56.100 --> 00:08:00.350
picks up the Mona Lisa and runs out of the room.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.491
Marcel runs for a long time.

00:08:03.551 --> 00:08:09.363
He thinks, "I want to leave the Mona Lisa somewhere safe, but where?"

00:08:09.423 --> 00:08:13.974
Then, after twenty minutes, he stops in a quiet street.

00:08:14.034 --> 00:08:17.036
In front of him there is a police station.

00:08:17.096 --> 00:08:19.536
The front door has a letter-box.

00:08:19.596 --> 00:08:22.587
"Of course!" Marcel thinks. "That's it."

00:08:22.647 --> 00:08:28.422
He stands up tall. Then he pushes the Mona Lisa through the letter-box.

00:08:28.482 --> 00:08:32.375
Two days later Marcel is in Paris again.

00:08:32.435 --> 00:08:35.000
At the station he sees a newspaper.

00:08:35.176 --> 00:08:39.777
It says, "ITALIAN POLICE FIND THE MONA LISA."

00:08:39.837 --> 00:08:43.900
Then he goes to the Louvre and tells Céline everything.

00:08:44.298 --> 00:08:46.479
"Oh, Nine cats!" she says.

00:08:46.539 --> 00:08:51.466
"Oh Marcel, are you all right?"

00:08:51.526 --> 00:08:54.957
"Yes, I'm fine," Marcel answers.

00:08:55.017 --> 00:08:57.231
He goes to Céline's window.

00:08:57.291 --> 00:09:00.888
"And the Mona Lisa's fine, too.

00:09:00.948 --> 00:09:05.000
Look, Céline." She's smiling.